// Naming gate — flags abbreviations and single-character bindings that Biome's
// `useNamingConvention` can't catch (it checks case, not length/abbreviation).
// Detection-only: agents see the diagnostic and rename. No autofix.
//
// Structure (named patterns + shared predicates, all in ONE plugin file so
// Biome compiles them into a single AST walk):
//
//   predicate is_abbreviation($id)               — the abbreviation dictionary, defined ONCE.
//                                                  Called by both the binding tier and the
//                                                  property-key tier, so the dictionary has a
//                                                  single source of truth (the prior form kept
//                                                  two byte-for-byte-identical regex copies that
//                                                  had to be hand-synced; that hazard is gone).
//   predicate flag_generic_iteration_name($id)   — the generic iteration-name list + the shared
//                                                  `info` diagnostic, defined ONCE. Called by both
//                                                  advisory patterns below.
//   pattern abbreviation_binding()               — dictionary hit on a const/let/var/param name.
//   pattern abbreviation_key()                   — dictionary hit on an object/type/class member key.
//   pattern single_char_binding()                — one-letter const/let/var/param name.
//   pattern single_char_key()                    — one-letter object/type/class member key.
//   pattern generic_iteration_callback_var()     — advisory: generic names in .map/.filter/… callbacks.
//   pattern generic_iteration_loop_var()         — advisory: generic names in for / for-of loop headers.
//   or { … }                                     — root: the six patterns composed together.
//
// `JsIdentifierBinding` is the declaration node, so the binding tiers are
// keyword-agnostic — const/let/var and function/callback parameters are covered
// uniformly. `JsLiteralMemberName` reaches the property-key shapes the binding
// node structurally cannot see (`{ n: … }`, `{ cnt: … }`, type/interface/class
// members). Registered via a scoped `overrides` entry in biome.jsonc that includes
// `**` but excludes `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx`: test files are intentionally exempt
// from naming discipline (a test's throwaway bindings and wire-format fixtures are
// not the code readers navigate). Widen or narrow that glob to change coverage — e.g.
// add more excludes to adopt the gate gradually as each directory is swept clean.
//
// The abbreviation set is ported from eslint-plugin-unicorn's prevent-
// abbreviations dictionary, MINUS a few sanctioned conventions (`err` catch
// bindings, `opts` options-object params) and a few ambiguous/high-false-positive
// short names that produce more noise than signal (`args`/`env` and similar).
// Single letters are handled by the single-char patterns below.
//
// TUNING — three separate knobs, do not confuse them:
//   • Project vocabulary  → the `is_allowlisted` predicate. Exempts a name from
//     EVERY tier. This is the one you want for a domain term or a public API field.
//     It ships empty; see the long note above it before adding anything.
//   • Abbreviation coverage → the `is_abbreviation` dictionary regex. One copy.
//   • Single-char exemptions → the `not $x <: r"…"` regex inside `single_char_binding`
//     / `single_char_key`. The binding tier exempts `_` and the conventional
//     single-char binding `z`; the key tier also exempts `e`. `i`/`j`/`k` are NOT
//     exempt in either tier — they are flagged everywhere (see naming-and-style.md
//     "Index and Counter Variables").
engine biome(1.0)
language js(typescript, jsx)

// **PERFORMANCE NOTE.** Every pattern below walks each identifier in every file.
// Optimisations applied:
//
//   1. The dictionary is a single anchored regex alternation `^(a|b|c)$`, not
//      `or { r"^a$", r"^b$", … }`. Modern regex engines build one DFA from the
//      alternation and match in one pass; the `or { … }` form evaluated each
//      alternative sequentially per identifier and was the single biggest hot spot.
//   2. That dictionary lives in ONE predicate (`is_abbreviation`) rather than being
//      duplicated across the binding and key tiers — one regex, compiled once.
//   3. Each single-char tier's exemption regex is anchored once.
//
// If a name slips that should be flagged, add it to the `^(...|...)$` alternation
// in `is_abbreviation` — DO NOT split it back into `or { r"...", r"..." }` because
// that re-introduces per-alternative evaluation cost.

// ── Shared predicates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Single source of truth for the abbreviation set. Called by both
// `abbreviation_binding` and `abbreviation_key`.
predicate is_abbreviation($identifier) {
  $identifier <: r"^(?:acc|amt|arr|attr|attrs|attType|auth|btn|buf|cb|cc|cfg|cn|cnt|conf|cr|ctx|cur|curr|cx|df|dir|dirs|dist|doc|docs|dst|el|elem|elems|ev|evt|ext|exts|func|hdr|idx|inp|len|lib|mod|msg|num|obj|out|pkg|qs|qty|req|res|ret|retval|sep|sig|sn|src|stdDev|str|tbl|td|temp|tit|tmp|ts|util|utils|val|vars|ver|win|bx|cmd|dec|dur|hi|lo|mem|prs|wf|sk|er)$"
}

// The gate's allowlist. Identifiers that must NEVER be flagged, regardless of the
// dictionary or the single-char tiers. Checked by every flagging tier via
// `not is_allowlisted(...)`, so a name here is exempt EVERYWHERE — bindings and
// keys, single- and multi-char.
//
// EMPTY BY DEFAULT, on purpose. This is the one part of the gate that cannot be
// shipped pre-filled: an allowlist is a list of a specific project's sanctioned
// vocabulary, and inheriting another project's list silently permits abbreviations
// that mean nothing here. (This blueprint's ancestor arrived carrying a LoRaWAN
// decoder's list — `rssi`, `fPort`, `gwId`, `ts`, `temp` — which would have made
// `ts` and `temp` legal everywhere in every project built from it.)
//
// The sentinel below matches no realistic identifier, so the allowlist starts
// closed. Two kinds of name legitimately belong here once your project has them:
//
//   • Domain vocabulary — an acronym that IS the correct name and has no longer
//     form to expand to (a protocol or standards term, not a shortening).
//   • Names fixed by an external contract — a public API field, a wire-format key,
//     or a map key that is itself parsed (e.g. `{ s: 1000, m: 60_000 }` where the
//     key string is the unit suffix). Renaming these breaks callers you cannot see.
//
// Add a name only with a RECEIPT — the published field, the spec term — never a
// guess, and never merely because the gate flagged it. Match the canonical name
// exactly (case-sensitive), and note that an entry exempts the name as a BINDING
// too, not just as a property key.
// `cn` is shadcn/ui's class-merge helper, imported under that exact name by the vendored
// components under packages/web/src/components (which are lint-excluded but resolve the
// import from our lib/utils.ts) — renaming it forks an ecosystem-wide convention.
predicate is_allowlisted($name) { $name <: r"^(?:cn)$" }

// Keys whose spelling is fixed by an EXTERNAL contract — a wire format or a
// third-party API's option bag. Exempt as property KEYS only; the same word is
// still flagged as a binding, so `const dir = …` in our own code keeps failing.
// That is the whole reason this is separate from `is_allowlisted` above, which
// exempts every tier: we owe the external shape its spelling, not ourselves.
//
// Each entry needs a RECEIPT naming the contract, same bar as the allowlist:
//   • `dir` — `Bun.serve`'s static directory-route option bag is `{ dir }`
//             (packages/web/src/server/dev-web.ts).
//
// `v` was the second entry — TanStack's `tanstack:interruptBinding` stamp — until #251
// retired it: #112 removed the run path the stamp belonged to, the receipt named a module
// (`packages/web/src/server/session.ts`) that no longer exists, and no first-party file
// spelled the key. An exemption whose leak has left is a hole nobody is watching, so the
// name is refused again by both single-character tiers.
//
// Replaces two per-line `// biome-ignore lint:` comments (#82). Those suppressed
// EVERY rule on their line; these exempt one name, in one tier, with a receipt.
//
// ⚠ Keyed on the NAME, so it reaches further than the line it replaced. That blast radius
// is bounded by `test/naming-gate.test.ts`, which reads THIS regex and holds it against the
// files that actually spell an exempted key — in both directions, so a third `{ dir: … }`
// and an exemption nothing relies on are equally a failing gate (PR #83 review, #251). That
// test also asserts the key/binding split, which is what breaks if this is ever folded into
// `is_allowlisted`.
predicate is_external_contract_key($name) { $name <: r"^(?:dir)$" }

// Single source of truth for the advisory tier: the generic iteration-name list
// AND the `info` diagnostic it emits. Called by both `generic_iteration_callback_var`
// and `generic_iteration_loop_var`, so the name list and the message live in ONE
// place (the prior form inlined the list in the callback tier only; the loop tier
// would otherwise have to re-state both).
predicate flag_generic_iteration_name($name) {
  $name <: r"^(?:index|count|value|result|data|item|entry|text|name|id|obj|arr)$",
  register_diagnostic(span=$name, message="Generic iteration variable — name what it walks (`sessions.map((s) => …)` → `(session) => …`, `for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; ...)` → `rowIndex`). Greppability wins in an agent codebase. See naming-and-style.md.", severity="info")
}

// ── Abbreviation tiers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A dictionary hit on a declared name (const/let/var/param/function/class).
pattern abbreviation_binding() {
  JsIdentifierBinding() as $name where {
    is_abbreviation($name),
    not is_allowlisted($name),
    register_diagnostic(span=$name, message="Abbreviated name — use the full word (config, context, request, response, message, callback, index, element, …). See naming-and-style.md.", severity="error")
  }
}

// A dictionary hit on an object-literal key, type/interface member, or class
// member name — the shapes the binding tier structurally cannot see (`{ ts: … }`).
pattern abbreviation_key() {
  JsLiteralMemberName() as $key where {
    is_abbreviation($key),
    not is_allowlisted($key),
    not is_external_contract_key($key),
    register_diagnostic(span=$key, message="Abbreviated property key — use the full word (`ts` → `timestamp`, `dir` → `directory`, `cmd` → `command`, `cnt` → `count`). See naming-and-style.md.", severity="error")
  }
}

// ── Single-character tiers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// One-letter declared name. Exempt: `_` and the conventional single-char binding
// `z`. `i`/`j`/`k` are flagged (not exempt) — name what the loop walks.
//
// ⚠ `error`, like every other FLAGGING tier, and that is load-bearing: `biome check` exits
// **0** on warnings, so the `warn` this carried until #251 reported `const v = 1` and landed
// it anyway, while the abbreviation tier beside it (`const dir = …`) blocked. Measured
// 2026-09-18 out-of-tree through the repo config: one-line fixture, "Found 1 warning",
// exit 0. Only the advisory `info` tier above is deliberately non-blocking, and it says so.
// `test/naming-gate.test.ts` now reads the SEVERITY of each diagnostic, not just its line,
// so a tier that reports without blocking is a failing gate.
pattern single_char_binding() {
  JsIdentifierBinding() as $name where {
    $name <: r"^[a-z]$",
    not $name <: r"^(?:_|z)$",
    not is_allowlisted($name),
    register_diagnostic(span=$name, message="Single-character name — use a descriptive name. Exempt: underscore, z. See naming-and-style.md.", severity="error")
  }
}

// One-letter object/type/class member key. Exempt: `_`, `z`, and `e`. `i`/`j`/`k`
// are flagged (not exempt) — a one-letter field name carries no meaning to a
// downstream reader (`{ n: … }` → `{ count: … }`).
pattern single_char_key() {
  JsLiteralMemberName() as $key where {
    $key <: r"^[a-z]$",
    not $key <: r"^(?:_|z|e)$",
    not is_allowlisted($key),
    not is_external_contract_key($key),
    register_diagnostic(span=$key, message="Single-character property key — use a descriptive field name (`{ n: … }` → `{ count: … }`). Exempt: _, z, e. See naming-and-style.md.", severity="error")
  }
}

// ── Advisory tier ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Generic iteration-variable names where the surrounding AST names a better one
// for free. Surfaces as `info` (does NOT fail CI) and is consumed by the
// PR-review workflow as a nit: the author acknowledges each (fix OR explicit
// wontfix) but is not required to act. Greppability wins in an agent-driven
// codebase, even at the cost of a few extra chars.
//
// Scoped to **iteration contexts** specifically: `.map(...)` / `.filter(...)` /
// `.find(...)` / `.forEach(...)` / `.some(...)` / `.every(...)` / `.flatMap(...)`
// callback params, the second param of `.reduce(...)` (the accumulated element,
// not the accumulator), and `for (…)` / `for (… of …)` loop headers. These are
// the shapes where the surrounding collection NAMES the better variable
// (`sessions.map((s) => …)` → `sessions.map((session) => …)`).
//
// Two patterns, because the two shapes match differently:
//   • Callbacks are matched with backtick code-snippet templates (expression
//     context — the snippet parser handles call expressions).
//   • Loop headers are matched with AST node patterns (`JsForStatement` /
//     `JsForOfStatement`). The snippet form `for (let $name = $_; …) $_` does NOT
//     match for-statements in Biome 2.4.16 — it parses without error but silently
//     fails to match (verified). Do NOT "simplify" these back to snippet templates.
//     `$init <: contains JsIdentifierBinding()` is scoped to the initializer
//     subtree, so it binds the loop variable and never the loop body's bindings.
//
// Kept intentionally narrow. A broader `JsIdentifierBinding` match was tried
// earlier and produced a high library-idiom false-positive floor (mostly
// framework/destructure idioms the iteration shape deliberately doesn't reach).
// If a new shape turns out to be high-signal and not covered here, add a template
// or node pattern rather than reverting to the broad binding match.
pattern generic_iteration_callback_var() {
  or {
    `$_.map(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.map($name => $_)`,
    `$_.map(($name, $_) => $_)`,
    `$_.filter(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.filter($name => $_)`,
    `$_.filter(($name, $_) => $_)`,
    `$_.find(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.find($name => $_)`,
    `$_.find(($name, $_) => $_)`,
    `$_.forEach(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.forEach($name => $_)`,
    `$_.forEach(($name, $_) => $_)`,
    `$_.some(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.some($name => $_)`,
    `$_.every(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.every($name => $_)`,
    `$_.flatMap(($name) => $_)`,
    `$_.flatMap($name => $_)`,
    `$_.reduce(($_, $name) => $_, $_)`,
    `$_.reduce(($_, $name) => $_)`
  } where { flag_generic_iteration_name($name) }
}

pattern generic_iteration_loop_var() {
  or {
    JsForStatement(initializer=$init),
    JsForOfStatement(initializer=$init)
  } where { $init <: contains JsIdentifierBinding() as $name, flag_generic_iteration_name($name) }
}

// ── Root composition ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
or {
  abbreviation_binding(),
  abbreviation_key(),
  single_char_binding(),
  single_char_key(),
  generic_iteration_callback_var(),
  generic_iteration_loop_var()
}
